{"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/obrio/96dce672-7b6c-4d97-8cc6-ecf75cafaf54":"[https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/03b1a010-37a9-4bc8-8902-7778974d90b3/b80eaf44-0470-410a-91a7-3a3c65ae7665/Frame%201321318777.png]\n\nПривіт!\n\nМи OBRIO — команда, яка завжди хоче більшого: від себе, від життя, від роботи. Якщо тобі теж замало «достатньо добре» — ти вже розумієш, про що ми. Тут сильні люди притягують сильних — і разом ми розвиваємо компанію, що будує продукт №1 у ніші spiritual wellness — Nebula.\n\nЗараз ми шукаємо Data Analyst до команди Payments.\n\nТи формуватимеш єдину картину платежів, на яку спирається компанія — від того, як конвертують платіжні методи в кожному ринку, до того, чи збігається прогноз у Tableau з грошима, які реально дійшли. Ця зона повністю твоя: логіка звірки, пороги алертів і модель прогнозу будуть такими, якими ти їх побудуєш — і саме на них компанія покладатиметься в грошових рішеннях.\n\nТи матимеш можливість попрацювати з командою сильних Payment-менеджерів, які тримають платіжну інфраструктуру, та з чотирма аналітиками у своїй безпосередній команді.\n\nТвоїм безпосереднім менеджером буде Олександра Рижова-Фоменко http://google.com/search?bih=698&biw=1470&ei=Jys5aoPUC9WswPAP8b3zGA&gs_lp=Egxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAiMNC-0LvQtdC60YHQsNC90LTRgNCwINGA0LjQttC-0LLQsCDRhNC-&oq=%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%B0+%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B6%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0+%D1%84%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BB&q=%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%B0+%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B6%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0+%D1%84%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BB&sca_esv=a34ddc620dd62935&sclient=gws-wiz-serp&sxsrf=APpeQnvd6Xou3y1KSEvbFXLMjVlv-Sy26g%3A1782131495197&uact=5&ved=0ahUKEwjDg9uV7ZqVAxVVFhAIHfHeHAMQ4dUDCBI, Team Lead Marketing Analystics.\n\nЯкі виклики тебе чекають?\n\n - Ти прогнозуватимеш ризик там, де немає історії — у нових локалях відсутній baseline, і рішення про запуск ринку спиратимуться на твою оцінку, а не на дані попередніх періодів\n\n - Ти будеш будувати структуру в зоні, де її ще немає: логіка звірки, пороги алертів і сама пріоритизація — все це тобі доведеться визначати самостійно\n\n - Ти візьмеш під контроль ризик-метрики, насамперед VAMP — розбереш, що на нього впливає, і системно знижуватимеш його замість реагування на вже сталі проблеми\n\nТвій вплив:\n\n - У побудові єдиної картини платежів — аналітиці конверсії платіжних методів по ринках, платіжному міксі та оцінці ризику при відкритті локалей без історії покупок\n\n - У контролі unit-економіки платежів — refund rate, rev share і податків: від пошуку причин відхилень до зменшення втрат\n\n - У володінні ризик-метриками, насамперед VAMP — від розуміння драйверів до системного покращення показника\n\n - У побудові алертингу по платіжній зоні, щоб ризики та збої проявлялись раніше, ніж завдають шкоди\n\n - У revenue-репортингу та прогнозуванні в Tableau, які збігаються з реальними грошима\n\nЩо для нас важливо?\n\n - Ти маєш 2+ роки досвіду в аналітиці — і розумієш, як влаштована економіка платежів: конверсія, refund rate, rev share, ризик-метрики\n\n - Впевнено пишеш SQL: складні запити, оптимізація, робота з великими таблицями\n\n - Використовуєш Python + pandas для аналізу, обробки даних і автоматизації\n\n - Знаєш статистичні методи і вмієш перетворювати дані на інсайти, а не просто на таблиці\n\n - Маєш досвід роботи з BI-інструментами — вмієш будувати дашборди, якими реально користуються\n\n - Ти помічаєш ту розбіжність, яку не бачить ніхто інший, і не пропускаєш її далі\n\n - Ти будуєш структуру там, де її немає, і сам пріоритизуєш, коли задачі ніхто не ставить\n\n - Ти впізнаєш себе в цінностях OBRIO https://obrio.co/about — GREAT\n\n - AI — вже частина того, як ти працюєш. Ти перевіряєш згенеровані запити та логіку звірки на джерелі, розпізнаєш правдоподібну, але хибну відповідь, і жодне число не потрапляє на дашборд без розуміння, як воно отримане. У нас працюють з Claude · Cursor · CodeRabbit · OpenRouter · AWS Bedrock · NotebookLM · N8N · Gemini · OpenAI · HeyGen · Arcads · Krea · Runway · Kling · ElevenLabs\n\nЩо ти отримаєш в OBRIO?\n\n - Свободу у форматі роботи — можливість працювати з офісу в Києві, Львові, Варшаві або remote, з підтримкою надкомфортних умов у трьох містах.\n\n - Сильне середовище для зростання — 75% команди формують Middle та Senior спеціалісти, тож ти швидко зростаєш через складні задачі та сильних колег.\n\n - Підтримку фізичного та ментального ресурсу — участь в OBRIO Wellness Club або покриття індивідуальних занять спортом та Spiritual Allowance для твого балансу (дивись, як це працює в нас https://www.instagram.com/p/DPWQRsIjK7i/?img_index=1&igsh=NWZhdjVqeXo3M2dr).\n\n - AI Workation — до 5 робочих днів на квартал, які ти можеш повністю присвятити створенню масштабованих AI-інструментів.\n\n - Час на відновлення — 20 оплачуваних днів відпустки, необмежені лікарняні та можливість sabbatical leave. Щоб досягати якнайкращих результатів потрібно якнайкраще почуватись.\n\n - Причетність до соціально важливих ініціатив — участь у благодійних проєктах, волонтерстві та підтримці мобілізованих колег і їхніх сімей. Один з наших проєктів OBRIO Innovation Space x КПІ https://www.instagram.com/reel/DJ9JTwUsLjA/?igsh=azlsMmM3cndsZTZm нещодавно номінований на DOU Awards.\n\n - Інвестиції у твій професійний розвиток — окремий бюджет на навчання, менторство та участь у топових українських і міжнародних конференціях (IT Arena, DOU Days, Web Summit, TikTok & Meta Summits).\n\n - Круті колаборації — об'єднуємось з українськими брендами (СЕНС, Matcher, Syndicat, KURAZH) і даруємо стильний OBRIO-мерч не лише з нагоди святкових дат.\n\nМи — OBRIO, продуктова IT-компанія з екосистеми Genesis, яка створює Nebula — найбільший spirituality бренд із 70M+ користувачів. З вісьмох ентузіастів ми виросли у команду з 300+ професіоналів, які створюють рішення, що впливають на життя людей у всьому світі.\n\n - OBRIO — Lovemark brand з найвищим eNPS за версією Forbes https://www.instagram.com/p/DJB0OhnMlAI/\n\n - За 7+ років наш продукт Nebula виріс з ідеї у платформу і став частиною життя мільйонів користувачів у понад 60 країнах\n\n - На платформі працюють 1500+ експертів. Ми створили складну операційну модель і щодня обробляємо тисячі запитів від користувачів по всьому світу\n\nАмбіція OBRIO — стати першим українським юнікорном у ніші spirituality.\n\nЯк виглядає наша hiring journey?\n\nІнтро-кол з TA Specialist → Оцінка навичок → Інтерв'ю з менеджером → Бар-рейзинг / Фінальне інтерв'ю → Job Offer\n\nУ тестових завданнях є блок на використання AI — при оцінці ми спираємось на 4D Framework від Anthropic https://www-cdn.anthropic.com/334975cdec18f744b4fa511dc8518bd8d119d29d.pdf?ref=hackshackers.com. Для нас важливе критичне й усвідомлене використання AI-інструментів.\n\nDo Big. Be Great.\n\n[https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/03b1a010-37a9-4bc8-8902-7778974d90b3/824a9c7e-3388-4966-88e8-3fa772331330/Refer%20your%20friends%20through%20our%20Hiring%20Bot%20and%20get%20bonuses%20Junior%20-%20300$%20Middle%20-%20600$%20Senior%20-%201000$%20LeadHead%20-%201500$.png]","https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/openart/3dad78e1-8e1f-4dc6-b042-3537b4beec46":"SOFTWARE ENGINEER, AGENT\n\n\n\n\n🎨 ABOUT OPENART\n\nOpenArt is an AI storytelling and visual creation platform used by millions of creators worldwide. We're building the next generation of creative tools powered by cutting-edge AI — enabling anyone to create videos, visuals, characters, and stories with unprecedented speed and imagination.\n\nWe believe the future of creativity is AI-native, and we're shaping that future.\n\n\n\n\n🚀 WHY JOIN OPENART\n\n - Ground floor of a new category — help define what \"agent\" means for creative work, the way Director redefined what \"directing\" means for video.\n\n - Small team, massive surface area — engineers own real systems end to end, not slices.\n\n - Real scale, real stakes — your agents run for millions of creators, and what you ship shows up in the product within days.\n\n - Founder-led engineering culture — both founders are technical and deeply involved in product and architecture.\n\n - AI-native product — you'll help decide how frontier models get orchestrated and exposed as experiences that feel effortless rather than technical.\n\n - High ownership, low process — we value judgment, clarity, and speed over bureaucracy.\n   \n   \n\n\n🎯 ABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe're hiring engineers to build the agent layer behind OpenArt's next generation of creative products, starting with Director — which lets anyone \"vibe direct\" a multi-minute cinematic video by chatting with AI. You'll be building the agent infrastructure that pushes experiences like this further: longer-horizon planning, tool use across multiple model vendors, memory across sessions, and the harness that keeps all of it reliable in production.\n\nThis isn't a research role — it's a product-and-systems role. You'll build on and extend the agent harness (tool use, context management, multi-step planning, evaluation), develop the MCP servers and CLI tooling around it, and ship the frontend experiences that make all of it feel effortless rather than technical. You'll work closely with the founders, the agent team, and design to turn \"what should this agent be able to do\" into a system that actually does it — reliably, at scale.\n\n\n\n\n🛠 WHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build and extend the agent harness that powers OpenArt's conversational and autonomous creative workflows: tool use, context/memory management, multi-step planning, and sub-agent orchestration\n\n - Build and maintain MCP servers and CLI-based agent tooling that connect our agents to internal services, external model vendors, and creative asset pipelines\n\n - Author reusable Agent Skills and structured workflows that let agents reliably handle complex, multi-step creative tasks — scene planning, storyboarding, asset generation, revision loops\n\n - Contribute to evaluation frameworks and observability so the team knows when an agent is working well, and can catch regressions before users do\n\n - Ship polished, production frontend experiences (React/Next.js) for agent-driven products, end to end\n\n - Make pragmatic trade-offs between speed, correctness, and scalability — and communicate them clearly\n\n - Partner closely with product, design, and GTM to translate user needs into technical solutions\n\n - Track the fast-moving agent ecosystem (MCP, Agent Skills, orchestration frameworks) and bring the best of it into OpenArt's stack\n   \n   \n\n\n⚙ WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\nCore Requirements\n\n - 2+ years of full-stack engineering experience shipping production software\n\n - Hands-on experience building LLM-powered agents or applications that have reached real users — not just prototypes or demos\n\n - Working familiarity with agent harness concepts: tool use, context/memory management, multi-step planning, or sub-agent orchestration\n\n - Solid data modeling and schema design skills for real product use cases\n\n - A strong AI-assisted coding practice — you use tools like Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor as a core part of how you build, and have real opinions about what makes them work well\n\n - Product sense — you think about what makes an agent experience feel trustworthy and delightful, not just functional\n\n - Clear communication — you can explain agent behavior and technical trade-offs to teammates who aren't engineers\n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience authoring reusable Agent Skills or structured agent workflows\n\n - Practical experience building MCP servers or CLI tooling for agents\n\n - Exposure to agent orchestration frameworks (Claude Agent SDK, LangGraph, or similar) or LLM evaluation / observability tooling\n\n - Hands-on experience with image / video generation models\n\n - Startup experience, or having built something 0 to 1 (side projects count)\n   \n   \n\n\n💰 COMPENSATION\n\n - $300k+ total compensation including base salary, bonus, equity\n\n - Equity - meaningful ownership in what you build\n\n - High autonomy, high growth environment\n   \n   \n\n\n🌍 WORK SETUP\n\n - Bay Area preferred (hybrid available)\n\n - Visa sponsorship available\n   \n   \n\n\n🎯 WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE IN 3–6 MONTHS\n\n - You've shipped a production agent workflow inside OpenArt's ecosystem, and real users are running it\n\n - You've meaningfully improved a piece of the harness, a set of Agent Skills, or the eval loop — and can point to the metric that moved\n\n - You own at least one part of the agent stack end to end and are the go-to person for it\n\n - You've formed a tight feedback loop with design, founders, and real users\n\n - You're proposing improvements and catching problems early, not just executing on specs\n\nIf you want to build the agents that turn frontier models into creative tools millions of people use — and grow fast while doing it — we'd love to talk.","https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/warp/718d38f5-dc6c-43cd-b7e5-ce70eab048d6":"ABOUT WARP\n\nWarp is the AI-native Employee Management Platform for ambitious companies. HRIS, payroll, benefits, IT, tax compliance, and more, all built from scratch on one AI-native platform.\n\nEvery company runs on its people, and the software that manages them is some of the oldest in the enterprise. Incumbents like ADP and Workday built their businesses on complexity and large ops teams. Warp is built for AI to be the primary operator. Every advance in LLM capability widens our lead.\n\nWe process $X billion in annual payments for high-growth companies across all 50 US states + globally.\n\nWe've raised $85M from Battery Ventures, Sapphire Ventures, Peak XV, Sound Ventures (Ashton Kutcher), and Y Combinator, alongside operators including Tobi Lütke (Shopify), Claire Hughes Johnson (Stripe), and the founders of Dropbox and Replit. Our team comes from MIT, Ramp, Brex, Google, Gusto, Rippling, and more.\n\nWe hire people who ship constantly, own outcomes, and care about craft. If you want to automate an entire category of work that every company depends on, this is the place.\n\nAbout the Role\nHigh-growth companies spend thousands of hours on people operations: onboarding new hires, running payroll, managing benefits, provisioning devices, answering policy questions, approving time off and expenses. Most of that work still runs on spreadsheets, tickets, and people chasing people. We're building agents that do it for them.\nWarp Agent works in the background for HR, finance, and people teams. It gets new hires ready for day one, reviews expenses against policy, handles time-off requests, checks payroll before it runs, and reports on what's happening across the company. Customers hand it a receipt or a notice and it takes care of the rest. Because Warp runs the full employee lifecycle on one platform, the agent has the context to finish the work, not just suggest it.\nThe hard part is trust. People data is the most sensitive data a company has, and people operations leave little room for error. Every agent action respects role-based permissions, so an IT manager's agent can provision a laptop without ever seeing anyone's salary, and every action is logged and auditable.\nWe believe agents will soon do more work on Warp than people do. As an Applied AI Engineer, you'll build those agents, the runtime they operate on, and the systems that make them reliable enough to run a company's people operations.\n\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n - Ship agentic features end to end, from the model call to the UI, across HRIS, payroll, benefits, IT, and more\n\n - Build and extend Warp Agent's harness: tool-calling, durable execution for long-running work (triggers, scheduling, wait and resume), and a run log that makes every agent action auditable\n\n - Design evals and guardrails for workflows where mistakes are costly, and decide when an agent acts on its own versus asks for approval\n\n - Build new agent workflows and expand what customers can configure and author themselves\n\n - Extend our permission model to agents so every action respects who the agent is working for\n\n - Build internal agents and tooling that remove manual work across Warp's own teams\n\n - Build new surfaces for interactions with Warp agent across the web app, employee app, mobile app, and slack\n\n - Collaborate directly with the CTO and CEO\n\nYou'll Be Good for This Role If You\n\n - Have shipped LLM features that real users depend on in production, and know where they break\n\n - Think in systems: evals, observability, cost, latency, and failure modes\n\n - Are product-minded and care how an agent's work shows up for the person who delegated it\n\n - Get excited by hard domains where correctness matters more than demos\n\n - Use coding agents heavily in your own workflow and have opinions on what works\n\nWhat You Need\n\n - Strong full-stack engineering skills and expertise in a modern, strongly typed language\n\n - A track record of building production AI systems: agents, tool use, retrieval, or structured extraction\n\n - Experience designing reliable backend systems\n\n - High agency. You figure things out.\n\n - Willingness to work from our NYC office five days a week\n\n\nBENEFITS AT WARP: \n\n - 100% Health Coverage: Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans for you and your dependents.\n\n - 401(k) Matching: Start investing in your future from day one.\n\n - Unlimited PTO: We offer flexible PTO, meaning you’re trusted to take the time you need to recharge while balancing your responsibilities and team commitments.\n\n - Commuter Benefits: Pre-tax commuter benefits for your daily trip to our NYC office.\n\n - Catered Lunch Daily: Great food, every day, on us. No meal prep, no decision fatigue.\n\n - Quarterly Offsites: Beautiful locations to connect as a team. Past locations include Spain, Catskills, and San Francisco.\n\nWarp is based in New York City, and most of our team works together in-office 5x per week. Please refer to the top of this page for this position's hiring location and working model.","https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/hpiq/jobs/6176783004":"Who We Are\nHP IQ is HP’s new AI innovation lab. Combining startup agility with HP’s global scale, we’re building intelligent technologies that redefine how the world works, creates, and collaborates.\nWe’re assembling a diverse, world-class team—engineers, designers, researchers, and product minds—focused on creating an intelligent ecosystem across HP’s portfolio. Together, we’re developing intuitive, adaptive solutions that spark creativity, boost productivity, and make collaboration seamless.\nWe create breakthrough solutions that make complex tasks feel effortless, teamwork more natural, and ideas more impactful—always with a human-centric mindset.\nBy embedding AI advancements into every HP product and service, we’re expanding what’s possible for individuals, organisations, and the future of work.\nJoin us as we reinvent work, so people everywhere can do their best work.\nAbout The Role\nHP IQ's Connectivity Software team is building foundational software that enables the next generation of connected experiences across devices and platforms. Our team works at the intersection of systems software, wireless connectivity, and emerging technologies to create seamless, intelligent experiences. We are looking for an Intern to join the team and contribute to the software, protocols, and systems that bring these experiences to life.\nIn this role, you will work alongside experienced engineers to develop on-device software for next-generation HP IQ experiences. You’ll contribute to the design, development, and implementation of software across emerging devices and platforms. This is a hands-on technical role where you’ll write code, solve complex system-level problems, and collaborate with engineers to explore and build new experiences.\nWhat You Might Do\nDevelop on-device firmware and system software in C, C++, or Python for connected device experiences.\nBuild and enhance software supporting wireless connectivity across a variety of devices and platforms.\nExplore sensing, machine learning, and AI techniques to solve complex technical challenges.\nDebug and resolve issues across system software, wireless connectivity, and application-level code.\nCollaborate with hardware and software engineers to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nParticipate in code reviews and technical design discussions, learning from and contributing to the broader engineering team.\nContribute to the testing, validation, and documentation of software and firmware features.\nEssential Qualifications\nWrite efficient on-device firmware and system software in C, C++, or Python to implement wireless connectivity protocols (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth) across multiple device types.\nDesign and implement device-to-device discovery and pairing protocols that enable seamless communication in enterprise and consumer environments.\nOptimize machine learning inference on resource-constrained devices, balancing model accuracy against power consumption and latency constraints.\nDevelop sensing algorithms that leverage data and AI techniques to enable new ambient and wearable interactions.\nDebug and resolve complex issues spanning the wireless stack, operating system integration, and application-level code.\nCollaborate with hardware engineers, system software teams, and product managers to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nParticipate in code reviews and design discussions, learning from and contributing insights to the team's technical direction.\nContribute to testing, validation, and documentation of connectivity features and firmware updates.\nPreferred Skills\nPrevious experience with edge machine learning or AI inference on embedded devices.\nFamiliarity with IoT or ambient computing paradigms.\nExperience shipping consumer software products from development through production.\nBackground in IoT, wearable, or mobile device development.\nExposure to agentic workflows or multi-device ecosystem design.\nHourly Pay Range: $45.00–$51.00 per hour. Actual compensation will be determined based on factors such as skills, qualifications, and experience.\n2027 Internship Program Dates: May/June–August/September 2027. Final dates will be based on student schedules.\nCompensation & Benefits (Full-Time Employees)\nThe salary range for this role is listed above. Final salary offered is based upon multiple factors including individual job-related qualifications, education, experience, knowledge and skills.\nAt HP IQ, we offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package, including:\nHealth insurance\nDental insurance\nVision insurance\nLong term/short term disability insurance\nEmployee assistance program\nFlexible spending account\nLife insurance\nGenerous time off policies, including;\n4-12 weeks fully paid parental leave based on tenure\n11 paid holidays\nAdditional flexible paid vacation and sick leave ( US benefits overview )\nWhy HP IQ?\nHP IQ is HP’s new AI innovation lab, building the intelligence to empower humanity—reimagining how we work, create, and connect to shape the future of work.\nInnovative Work\nHelp shape the future of intelligent computing and workplace transformation.\nAutonomy and Agility\nWork with the speed and focus of a startup, backed by HP’s scale.\nMeaningful Impact\nBuild AI-powered solutions that help people and organisations thrive.\nFlexible Work Environment\nFreedom and flexibility to do your best work.\nForward-Thinking Culture\nWe learn fast, stay future-focused, and imagine what comes next—together.\nEqual Opportunity Employer (EEO) Statement\nHP, Inc. provides equal employment opportunity to all employees and prospective employees, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, sexual orientation, age, disability, or status as a protected veteran, marital status, familial status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic predisposition or carrier status, uniformed service status, political affiliation or any other characteristic protected by applicable national, federal, state, and local law(s).\nPlease be assured that you will not be subject to any adverse treatment if you choose to disclose the information requested. This information is provided voluntarily. The information obtained will be kept in strict confidence.\nIf you’d like more information about HP’s EEO Policy or your EEO rights as an applicant under the law, please click here: Equal Employment Opportunity is the Law Equal Employment Opportunity is the Law – Supplement","https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/evolutioniq/jobs/6210230004":"About Us:  EvolutionIQ’s mission is to deliver state of the art technology that helps insurance claims teams make claims handling more accurate, fair, and efficient, so that more people impacted by injury or illness can continue their lives with dignity and stability. We are currently experiencing massive growth and to accomplish our goals, we are hiring world-class talent who want to help build and scale internally, and transform the insurance space. Our team is our #1 priority, and we have been named one of Inc.’s Best Workplaces 3 years in a row and Built In’s Best Places to work in 2025 and 2026!\nAbout You: An ambitious Associate Data Engineer who wants to jumpstart their career by diving into the core of our technical operations. You have a passion for problem-solving, data analytics, and ensuring customer requests are handled seamlessly from start to finish. You are excited to take on hands-on ticket work, collaborating closely with our Solutions Engineering team to uncover insights and drive cross-functional initiatives. You love investigating issues, analyzing data, and learning how to reduce friction in the engineering and client experience.\nIn this Role You Will:\nTake ownership of incoming technical tickets, investigating issues, and driving them to resolution to ensure a seamless customer experience.\nCollaborate daily with Solutions Engineers to run analytics, extract data insights, and support strategic client deliverables.\nAct as a technical liaison providing cross-functional support between Technical Support, Product Management, and Engineering to ensure requests flow smoothly through their lifecycle.\nHelp measure and track SLAs (e.g., 1 business day for triage, 5 business days for review) and proactively unblock stalled requests.\nAssist in identifying trends from ticket data to inform product improvements and engineering priorities.\nLearn and grow within the engineering space, collaborating directly with cross-functional teams like DevOps and Client Strategy and Analytics.\nRequirements:\n0-2 years of experience in software engineering, technical support, IT operations, data analytics, or a similar technical role (recent graduates with strong internship experience are welcome).\nBasic proficiency in Python and SQL (or similar querying/scripting languages) to support data analytics and technical investigations.\nFamiliarity with standard issue-tracking platforms and support workflows.\nConceptual understanding of the software development life cycle, Agile planning, and client support best practices.\nHigh attention to detail and a data-driven mindset to parse through logs, metrics, and customer reports.\nYou have crisp written and verbal communication skills and the ability to effectively translate technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders (like Client Services and customers).\nExcellent collaboration skills and a team-player attitude, open to giving and receiving critical feedback across teams.\nWork-life, Culture & Perks:\nCompensation: The base salary range is $100-125K, with flexibility depending on a candidate’s background and experience. Plus annual bonus plan\nWell-Being: Medical, dental, vision, short & long-term disability, life insurance and AD&D, and 401k matching. Additional family, wellness, and pet benefits.\nHome & Family: Paid time off and sick leave, 100% paid parental leave (16 weeks for primary caregivers and 12 weeks for secondary caregivers). We offer a flexible schedule for new parents returning to work.\nOffice Life: Catered lunches, happy hours, pet-friendly spaces, and monthly technology stipend.\nGrowth & Training: $1,000/year for each employee for professional development, as well opportunities for tuition reimbursement.\nEvolutionIQ appreciates your interest in our company as a place of employment. EvolutionIQ is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees."}
